[310.05871, "o", "stem outside the container namespace, so they are not directly accessible inside the container filesystem unless mounted or via dev.\\nWait! Is `main.\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdb-wal\u001b[m\u001b[K` completely gone from userland, or was it unlinked in the overlayfs?\\nWait, when a file is unlinked on overlayfs upperdir, it creates a character device 0,0 (whiteout file `.wh.main.\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdb-wal\u001b[m\u001b[K`).\\nCan we check if there's any file in `/app` or hidden files or if we can recover unlinked file or undelete, or maybe check deleted files on ext4 disk?\\nWait! Look at `/dev/vda` mounted on `/etc/hosts` etc.\\\",\\n  \\\"plan\\\": \\\"Check `ls -la /app` including hidden files, and check `/tmp` or history or ext4 extundelete/fls/icat if available or python process memory.\\\",\\n  \\\"commands\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"keystrokes\\\": \\\"ls -la /app; Which ext4magic extundelete fls icat 2>/dev/null; history | tail -n 20\\\\n\\\",\\n      \\\"duration\\\": 0.5\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\",\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[K/logs/agent/trajectory.json\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K            \"content\": \"New Terminal Output:\\n\\nroot@0bf9b3ba5bce:/app# ls -la /app; which ext4magic extundelete fls icat 2>/dev/null; history | tail -n 20\\ntotal 20\\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root root 4096 Aug 12 15:20 .\\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root root 4096 Aug 12 15:20 ..\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 8192 Oct 24  2025 main.db\\n    1  clear\\n    2  ls -la /app\\n    3  python3 -c \\\"import sqlite3; conn = sqlite3.connect('/app/main.db'); print('Tables:', conn.execute(\\\\\\\"SELECT name FROM sqlite_master WHERE type='table'\\\\\\\").\\nfetchall()); print('Count:', conn.execute('SELECT count(*) FROM \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kitem\u001b[m\u001b[Ks').fetchall()); print('Rows:', conn.execute('SELECT * FROM \u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kitem\u001b[m\u001b[Ks').fetchall())\\\"\\n    4  xxd /app/main.\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdb-wal\u001b[m\u001b[K | head -n 30\\n    5  ls -la /app\\n    6  find