/cwd` or `/proc/*/fd/*` or `/proc/*/maps` or `/proc/*/mem` or trash/tmp/journal or overlayfs whiteouts!\\nWait! In overlayfs, when a file in upperdir is deleted or when a lower file is deleted, a whiteout `.wh.main.\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdb-wal\u001b[m\u001b[K` is created in upperdir.\\nWait! Where is upperdir or how can we access lowerdir/upperdir or un-whiteout or read from debugfs / ext4 journal or filesystem?\\nWait! Is debugfs or e2fsprogs installed?\\\",\\n  \\\"plan\\\": \\\"Check if debugfs, e2fsprogs, testdisk, or other utilities are available.\\\",\\n  \\\"commands\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"keystrokes\\\": \\\"which debugfs e2fsutils testdisk lsof fuser 2>/dev/null\\\\n\\\",\\n      \\\"duration\\\": 0.5\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\",\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[K/logs/agent/trajectory.json\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K            \"content\": \"Previous response had parsing errors:\\nERROR: Invalid JSON: Invalid control character at: line 2 column 65 (char 66) | Content preview: '{\\\\n  \\\"analysis\\\": \\\"Wait! Where was `main.\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdb-wal\u001b[m\u001b[K` located originally?\\\\nWhen the session started, the ter'...\\n\\nPlease fix these issues and provide a proper JSON response.\"\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[K/logs/agent/trajectory.json\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K      \"message\": \"Analysis: When the session started, main.db (8192 bytes) and main.\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdb-wal\u001b[m\u001b[K (16512 bytes) were in /app. When python connected, SQLite deleted main.\u001b[01;31m\u001b[Kdb-wal\u001b[m\u001b[K. Let's see if debugfs or testdisk or lsof are available to inspect the filesystem/journal or undelete.\\nPlan: Check for available filesystem tools like debugfs, testdisk, lsof.\",\r\n\u001b[35m\u001b[K/logs/agent/trajectory.json\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[K:\u001b[m\u001b[K      \"message\": \"{\\n  \\\"analysis\\\": \\\"`/dev/vda` cannot be opened directly due to container privileges (`Operation not permitted`)